stars.csv is derived from the HYG Database v4.1 by David Nash (astronexus),
https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Filtered to magnitude 6.5 and brighter. stars-faint.bin is the same data from
magnitude 6.5 to 9, in a compact form.

milkyway.png is also derived from the HYG Database: it is the smoothed density
of its stars from magnitude 6.5 to 11, so it shows where stars are concentrated,
not a photograph or a measurement of the sky's real brightness.

deepsky.csv is derived from OpenNGC by Mattia Verga,
https://github.com/mattiaverga/OpenNGC, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Filtered to Messier objects and objects of magnitude 11 and brighter.

These derived files are also licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.

